# Nucleus Project Rules (v4.1)

**Status**: Design locked at v4.1, pre-implementation. PoC #1 (Dagster Error Translation) starts next. No production code yet.

**Source of truth**: `nucleus_architecture_v4.1.md` (supersedes v4.0 and v3; both deprecated). Read `AGENTS.md` at repo root for full required reading order.

## Project Identity (1 sentence)

**Nucleus ships data products from a laptop** — a local-first Python SDK + CLI for building Iceberg-native pipelines and analytics stacks, built on open Apache foundations, AI-ready by design. Grows with the team. Graduates cleanly to giants. *(Full positioning hierarchy + amendments: `docs/decisions/ADR-002-positioning-decision-2026-05.md`.)*

## Default Decision: WRAP, not BUILD

For every proposed component, ask: "Which production-grade OSS handles this already?"

| Concern | Default (wrap) | Swap target (interface + smoke tests only) | When available |
|---|---|---|---|
| SQL engine | DuckDB | Apache DataFusion | v0.1 |
| DataFrame engine | Polars | DataFusion DF | v0.1 |
| Multimodal/AI engine | Daft (optional) | — | v0.5+ |
| Vector storage | Lance / LanceDB | — | v0.5+ |
| Scheduling / orchestration | Dagster (embedded, hidden) | `nucleus-mini-scheduler` (in-house fallback by v1.0) | v0.1 |
| SQL transformations | **Native `ctx.sql` + Jinja** | dbt-duckdb (optional adapter v0.3) / SQLMesh | v0.1 |
| Connectors | **`ctx.copy_from` (v0.1)** / dlt (v0.3+) | Sling / Singer | v0.1 / v0.3 |
| Catalog | **Filesystem (v0.1)** / Lakekeeper (v0.3+) | Apache Polaris | v0.1 / v0.3 |
| Notebooks | Marimo | Jupyter | v0.3+ |
| Lineage | OpenLineage + sqlglot (asset-level v0.1; column-level v0.5+) | — | v0.1+ |
| **Auth → OIDC delegation (never own identity)** | Authentik / Keycloak / Okta / Azure AD | — | v0.3+ |
| Observability | OpenTelemetry + VictoriaMetrics + VictoriaLogs | — | v0.5+ |
| Table format (structured) | Apache Iceberg | (Tier 0, immortal) | v0.1 |
| Table format (multimodal) | Lance | (Tier 0, immortal) | v0.5+ |

**Build** only the experience and intelligence layers: `ctx` SDK, `nucleus` CLI, Workbench (v0.2+), Asset Materialization Adapter (~500 LOC), Error Translation Layer, native `ctx.sql` Jinja resolver (~1000 LOC), AI Copilot, Cost Meter. Total proprietary code budget ≤ **30K LOC** by v1.0.

## Eleven Hard Constraints (Non-Negotiable)

### Architectural Constraints

1. No JVM in core path
2. No public plugin SDK in v1
3. No custom scheduler (Dagster wrapped + mini-scheduler fallback by v1.0)
4. No custom compute engine
5. **No custom Iceberg commit service / transaction coordinator** (catalog handles atomic commits)
6. **No custom auth system** (always delegate to OIDC)
7. No ML platform / AI training / agent hosting platform
8. ≤ 30K LOC proprietary code by v1.0
9. Composability by Constitution: every Tier 1/2 dependency MUST have clean swap **interface** + smoke tests in CI; full adapter built on-demand only

### Operating Constraints

10. **Read official docs before integration.** Never rely on AI memory. Every wrapped component requires reading official docs before first integration AND before any version upgrade. See AGENTS.md §11.12.
11. **Upgrade-safe stack design.** Exact version pins in `pyproject.toml`, one-component-per-PR upgrades, mandatory upgrade smoke tests in CI, major version upgrades require ADR. See AGENTS.md §11.13.

## Composability by Constitution (Law #1) — v4.1 REVISED

Every Tier 1/2 dependency MUST have:
1. **Clean swap interface** (types compile, API surface matches) — ALWAYS maintained
2. **Basic smoke tests** (5-10 tests, not full E2E) — ALWAYS run in CI
3. **Full swap implementation** — built **on-demand** when trigger event fires (vendor death, license pivot, perf regression >2x, community demand)
4. Migration path documented in `/docs/swap/{component}.md`

Tier 0 (immortal) only: Apache Arrow, Iceberg, Parquet, Lance, S3 API, OpenLineage, OpenTelemetry.

**Do NOT** maintain full second implementations of every alternative pre-emptively. That is "Composability Tax" — avoid it.

## Beachhead (v0.1 through v1.0)

**Designed exclusively for: Startup data team — 5-20 engineers, 100GB-5TB total data, greenfield project.**

**v0.1 success metric:** 5-engineer team builds first BI-ready Iceberg table from `git clone` in **<30 minutes** via CLI.

Any feature that doesn't serve this metric is deferred. Other personas (solo, enterprise) are v1.5+.

## v0.1 Hello World Scope (Mo 0-4)

CLI-only. No Workbench. No AI Copilot. No Marimo. No dlt. No Lakekeeper.

In: ctx SDK core (read/write/sql/copy_from/log/params), DuckDB + Polars, Iceberg via pyiceberg + filesystem catalog, MinIO, Dagster wrapped + Error Translation Layer, native ctx.sql Jinja, ctx.copy_from helper, asset-level lineage, schema contracts, CLI (init/up/down/run/ingest).

Out: Everything else (defer to v0.2/0.3/0.5).

## Yield-to-Giants Strategy

We do NOT compete with Databricks/Snowflake. We integrate via three modes:

- **Mode 1**: Iceberg portability — user graduates with zero migration
- **Mode 2**: Hybrid compute — dispatch heavy assets to Databricks/Snowflake via `compute=...`
- **Mode 3**: Federation — Iceberg REST catalog federation for Data Mesh (v2.0+)

## Five Pillars (Frame All Decisions)

Every decision must serve ≥1 pillar without harming another:

1. High performance on minimal resources
2. Composable by constitution
3. AI-assisted by design
4. Familiar UX from proven giants
5. Friendly to giants, hostile to no-one

## 8-Question Gate for New Features

Before proposing anything new, all eight must be "yes":

1. Maps to one of the five architectural layers? (Physics / Engines / Coordination / Intelligence / Experience)
2. Serves the **<30 minute** beachhead metric (5-engineer team, `git clone` → BI-ready Iceberg table)?
3. Wrap possible instead of build?
4. Preserves no-JVM constraint?
5. Preserves local-identical-to-prod?
6. Stays within 30K LOC budget?
7. Triggered by empirical telemetry, not anxiety?
8. Required for v0.1 Hello World (Mo 0-4), or can it defer to v0.2/0.3/0.5?

A "no" or "unclear" anywhere → reject or defer.

